#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Render the exact N24 construction with locally bundled mathematics."""
from pathlib import Path
import json,html,re
HERE=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
ROOT=HERE.parents[2]
def tex(value,display=True):
 return '<div class="math" data-tex="'+html.escape(value,quote=True)+'" data-display="'+str(display).lower()+'"></div>'
def main():
 state=json.loads((HERE/'basis.json').read_text());c=json.loads((HERE/'certificate.json').read_text())
 assert json.loads((HERE/'verification.json').read_text())['passed']
 css=re.search(r'<style>(.*?)</style>',(ROOT/'research/t2-spin2-inertia/index.html').read_text(),re.S).group(1)
 css='\n'.join(line.rstrip() for line in css.split('\n'))
 css+=' .math{overflow-x:auto;max-width:100%;padding:.4rem 0}.scroll-table{overflow-x:auto}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%}td,th{text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid #deddd3;padding:.55rem}.integer{font-size:.74rem;white-space:nowrap}details{margin:1.3rem 0}summary{cursor:pointer}.downloads{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:.6rem}nav{display:flex;gap:1rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:1.5rem 0}'
 catalogue='../../../index.html#n=24&amp;t=2&amp;subspace=algebraic-n24-k5-t2'
 body='<p class="eyebrow">Anticoherent subspaces · Exact algebraic construction</p><a href="'+catalogue+'">← Return to the catalogue</a><h1>Twenty-four qubits at second order</h1><p class="lead">A cyclic-residue construction produces an exact five-dimensional AC subspace and attains the rigorous upper bound.</p><div class="result"><strong>Proved maximum</strong>'+tex(r'\boxed{K(24,2)=5}')+'<p>Every normalized complex superposition in the span is second-order AC.</p></div><nav><a href="#basis">Analytical basis</a><a href="#root">Exact coefficient definition</a><a href="#proof">Proof</a><a href="#files">Files</a></nav><section id="basis"><h2>Five residue classes, paired by reflection</h2><p>Use normalized Dicke states. Unitary reversal pairs the first and fifth vectors and the second and fourth; the middle vector is palindromic.</p>'+tex(state['derivationLatex'])+'<p>There is no complex conjugation in the reversal. The coefficients are exact algebraic numbers specified below. A shorter expression in radicals has not been established.</p>'+tex(state['parameterLatex'])+'<p><a href="basis.json">Download all exact coefficient expressions ↓</a> · <a href="'+catalogue+'">Explore the basis in the catalogue ↗</a></p></section>'
 body+='<section id="root"><h2>An explicit algebraic prescription</h2><p>Write the coefficient of the Dicke state with index r in vector a as</p>'+tex(r'c_{a,r}=\sqrt{\binom{24}{r}}\,\xi_{a,r},\qquad h_0(r)=1,\quad h_1(r)=24-2r,\quad h_2(r)=3(24-2r)^2-624.')+'<p>Insert the support and reflection relations above into these quadratic polynomials:</p>'+tex(r'P_{ab}^{q,p}(x)=\sum_{r=q}^{24}\binom{24}{r}r^{\underline q}h_p(r)\overline{\xi_{a,r-q}}\xi_{b,r}-\delta_{q0}\delta_{p0}\delta_{ab}.')+'<p>The Gram and first- and second-order moment conditions yield 42 nonzero real equations. Their exact rational coefficient rank is 23. The following 23 equations determine the 23 remaining real coordinates.</p><details><summary>The 23 defining equations</summary><div class="scroll-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Equation</th><th>Basis pair (a,b)</th><th>q</th><th>p</th><th>Part</th></tr></thead><tbody>'
 for i,e in enumerate(c['equations'],1):body+='<tr><td>F'+str(i)+' = 0</td><td>'+str(tuple(a+1 for a in e['basisPair']))+'</td><td>'+str(e['raisingPower'])+'</td><td>'+str(e['zPower'])+'</td><td>'+e['part']+'</td></tr>'
 body+='</tbody></table></div><p>The certificate gives every integer coefficient and an exact rational linear combination recovering each remaining equation.</p></details><p>Choose the unique real zero in the rational box</p>'+tex(r'|x_i-x_i^{(0)}|\le10^{-60},\qquad x_i^{(0)}=n_i/10^{80},\qquad i=1,\ldots,23.')+'<details><summary>Exact integer numerators of the isolating-box center</summary><p>These integers define the box; they do not replace the exact root by rounded coefficients.</p><div class="scroll-table"><table><thead><tr><th>i</th><th>nᵢ</th></tr></thead><tbody>'
 for i,slot in enumerate(c['unknownSlotIndices'],1):body+='<tr><td>'+str(i)+'</td><td class="integer">'+c['fullCenterNumerators'][slot]+'</td></tr>'
 body+='</tbody></table></div></details></section><section id="proof"><h2>Existence with exact arithmetic</h2><p>A rational preconditioner A gives the fixed-point map</p>'+tex(r'G(x)=x-AF(x).')+'<p>Integer and rational arithmetic verifies a strict contraction and strict containment of the image inside the box:</p>'+tex(r'\begin{aligned}\operatorname{Lip}(G)&<2.4\times10^{-51},\\\|G(x)-x^{(0)}\|_\infty&<5\times10^{-81}<10^{-60}.\end{aligned}')+'<p>The contraction theorem proves existence and uniqueness. The preconditioner is invertible, so the fixed point solves the defining equations. All 42 physical equations then follow from exact rational identities.</p><h2>The whole span is AC</h2><p>The full Gram and spin-moment equations are equivalent to</p>'+tex(r'R_2(|u_a\rangle\langle u_b|)=\delta_{ab}\frac{I_3}{3},\qquad 1\le a,b\le5.')+'<p>This includes all 225 reduced-state entries and every cross term between distinct basis vectors.</p><h2>Why five is optimal</h2><p>The general bound applies to every second-order AC subspace:</p>'+tex(r'5k\le N+5=29\quad\Longrightarrow\quad k\le5.')+'<p>The construction attains it. <a href="../../t2-spin2-inertia/index.html">Read the general upper-bound proof ↗</a></p><h2>What the construction establishes</h2><p>This is an exact optimal instance of the cyclic-residue prescription. Existence or optimality of the same prescription for every qubit number remains unproved.</p></section><section id="files"><h2>Proof and reproducibility</h2><div class="downloads">'
 for name,label in [('basis.json','Exact analytical basis'),('proof.tex','LaTeX proof'),('certificate.json','Rational root certificate'),('verify.py','Exact verifier'),('verification.json','Verification report')]:body+='<a href="'+name+'">'+label+' ↓</a>'
 body+='</div></section><footer><p>Catalogue calculation · 30 October 2026</p><a href="'+catalogue+'">Return to the catalogue ↗</a></footer>'
 head='<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Twenty-four qubits: optimal second-order AC subspace</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="../../../vendor/katex/katex.min.css"><script defer src="../../../vendor/katex/katex.min.js"></script><style>'+css+'</style><script>document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded",()=>document.querySelectorAll("[data-tex]").forEach(el=>{if(window.katex)el.innerHTML=katex.renderToString(el.dataset.tex,{displayMode:el.dataset.display==="true",throwOnError:false,strict:"ignore",trust:false});}));</script></head><body><main>'
 (HERE/'index.html').write_text(head+body+'</main></body></html>\n')
if __name__=='__main__':main()
